course: dictionary
lesson: 3822
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one the writer means. Read the context first. «When a table is laid, every person gets a knife, a fork and a spoon» tells you a fork is something you eat with.
explain: Fork can also be an action word. A road can fork, which means it splits into two parts going different ways. Ask yourself: is fork a thing, or is something happening?
explain: Be careful with «fork out». Nobody is eating or digging. The idea of money tells you it means to pay, often when you do not want to.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If «split into two» or «pay» still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A fork is a tool with a handle and two to four points, called prongs, that you use to eat food.
fact: A garden fork is a large tool with prongs for digging soil.
fact: A fork in a road or river is the place where it splits into two.
fact: To fork out means to pay money, often unwillingly. It is informal, so use it in chatty writing, not formal writing.
fact: «Snakes smell with their forked tongue»: forked means split into two points.
exercise: «When a table is laid, every person gets a knife, a fork and a spoon.» What is a fork in this sentence? | A kind of snake | A place where a road splits | A large tool for digging soil | *A tool with a handle and two to four prongs, for eating food
exercise: Leo says, «The road forks just past the church.» What does fork mean here? | Goes up a steep hill | Ends in a dead end | Gets very wide and flat | *Splits into two parts going different ways
exercise: Mum says, «We had to fork out for new school shoes.» What does fork out mean? | Eat something quickly | Split into two parts | *Pay money, often unwillingly | Dig up the soil
test: «Snakes smell with their forked tongue.» What does forked mean here? | Sticky and wet | *Split into two points | Very long and thin | Made of metal
test: Which sentence uses fork as an action word? | Please pass me the fork. | The garden fork is in the shed. | A tuning fork makes one exact note. | *The river forks just past the bridge.
exam: What does the sentence «You must never poke a knife or fork into a toaster, even when it is switched off at the wall» warn you about? | Forks are sharp, so keep them in a drawer | Toasters are good for cooking eggs | Always use a fork to check whether toast is ready | *Never put a fork into a toaster, even when it is switched off
